@*
    One confirmation modal per page, reused by every action that needs one. Bootstrap
    handles the focus trap and Escape; site.js focuses Cancel on open so a reflexive
    Enter takes the safe path, and fills in the wording from the trigger attributes.

    Never a bare browser confirm(): it cannot explain what will happen in more than one
    sentence, cannot style the destructive action red, and matches nothing else on screen.
*@
<div class="modal fade" id="pmsConfirmModal" tabindex="-1"
     aria-labelledby="pmsConfirmTitle" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">
                <h2 class="modal-title" id="pmsConfirmTitle" data-pms-confirm-title>Are you sure?</h2>
                <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal"
                        aria-label="Close without changing anything"></button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">
                <p data-pms-confirm-body></p>

                @*
                    An optional reason, shown only when the trigger asks for one with
                    data-pms-confirm-prompt. Module 5's cancellation needs it: "why was invoice
                    452 cancelled" is a question an owner asks about their own staff, so the
                    reason is collected at the moment of the decision rather than inferred
                    later. It lives here rather than on a page of its own because a destructive
                    action and its justification belong in the same breath.
                *@
                <div data-pms-confirm-prompt-field hidden>
                    <label class="pms-form-label pms-required" for="pmsConfirmPrompt"
                           data-pms-confirm-prompt-label></label>
                    <input type="text" class="form-control" id="pmsConfirmPrompt"
                           data-pms-confirm-prompt-input maxlength="500" autocomplete="off" />
                    <span class="pms-field-error" data-pms-confirm-prompt-error hidden>
                        A reason is required.
                    </span>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-footer">
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal"
                        data-pms-confirm-cancel>Cancel</button>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-danger" data-pms-confirm-ok>
                    <span class="pms-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>Confirm
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
